WEBVTT

00:01.036 --> 00:04.098
MERCEDES CAULIS

00:11.095 --> 00:14.074
ALBIS VINA
ELFARIA ALBIS SERFORT

00:15.025 --> 00:18.062
Could I have a moment, Lady Elfaria?

00:24.055 --> 00:25.057
Wake up.

00:28.005 --> 00:30.059
That hurts, Sarissa.

00:30.059 --> 00:31.051
Then,

00:31.051 --> 00:34.056
AIDE-DE-CAMP OF ICE FACTION - SARISSA ALFELD
please act in a way befitting a Magia Vander.

00:34.056 --> 00:37.081
You're always sleeping or looking
at the bottom of the Tower.

00:37.081 --> 00:41.081
You frivolous Magia Vander
in saint clothing.

00:43.036 --> 00:45.044
What do you want?

00:46.032 --> 00:49.007
Please take a moment to review these.

00:49.053 --> 00:52.045
These are the candidates
recommended by our scouts.

00:52.045 --> 00:54.053
Candidates?

00:54.053 --> 00:57.002
Yes. We have a nice harvest this year.

00:57.006 --> 01:01.096
And that one seems like an excellent
candidate for the Ice Faction.

01:02.037 --> 01:04.023
Julius Reinberg.

01:04.088 --> 01:07.071
He's making a performance
at the festival as we speak.

01:07.071 --> 01:12.005
He may suited to become
your successor, Lady Elfaria.

01:13.026 --> 01:19.098
Indeed, if he's as good as reported here,

01:20.039 --> 01:22.027
he may be able to become my successor.

02:46.001 --> 02:49.036
EPISODE 7: EL GLACE FROSSE

02:56.045 --> 02:59.053
Crown Attack has reached the finale!

02:59.053 --> 03:04.041
Whoever claims the crown on the podium
will get the glory!

03:04.041 --> 03:11.017
And right now, all three members of Squad 9
will face up against Will of Squad 6!

03:11.092 --> 03:14.038
I'm glad you made it, Flunkee.

03:14.097 --> 03:18.055
I was worried that
we would win just like this.

03:19.063 --> 03:23.056
If I didn't crush you
without humiliating you,

03:24.002 --> 03:27.006
I wouldn't be satisfied.

03:27.073 --> 03:29.094
Don't worry, Julius.

03:30.033 --> 03:35.035
I don't plan on losing before
you apologize to Donnan and others.

03:36.004 --> 03:39.057
That's big talk for a no-talent.

03:40.049 --> 03:45.046
From now on, you're nothing more than
a little rat for me to toy with.

03:52.021 --> 03:53.046
A smokescreen?

03:53.046 --> 03:55.034
I can sense their magic in there.

03:55.034 --> 03:57.038
Are they going to fire their spells?

04:00.009 --> 04:00.093
No.

04:04.097 --> 04:07.056
Footsteps.
They're moving.

04:07.056 --> 04:10.001
They're trying to surround me.

04:16.086 --> 04:19.028
If I don't keep moving, they'll get me.

04:19.028 --> 04:23.003
Even if my view is blocked,
I can detect where their spells come from.

04:25.024 --> 04:26.095
There's the second and third attack...

04:27.054 --> 04:30.058
I dodged all three of them.
Now I know where they are.

04:32.004 --> 04:33.013
I got you!

04:37.042 --> 04:39.018
A fourth one?!

04:43.051 --> 04:46.031
What are you doing, Flunkee?

04:46.093 --> 04:51.019
We haven't even moved one step.

04:55.027 --> 04:56.069
Hey, look at that!

05:06.091 --> 05:10.021
There are four, no, five Julius?

05:10.021 --> 05:13.033
Illusion? No, that's not it.

05:13.071 --> 05:15.071
Could it be...

05:15.071 --> 05:18.071
I forgot to mention it.

05:18.071 --> 05:21.009
That me over there explodes, you know?

05:21.009 --> 05:22.059
Eisplosion.

05:25.035 --> 05:26.035
Will!

05:32.073 --> 05:38.048
Will is frozen after getting caught
in a sudden explosion from that Julius!

05:38.048 --> 05:40.086
But rather than that,
what was that?

05:41.045 --> 05:42.061
That spell...

05:43.001 --> 05:44.099
There's no doubt about it.

05:47.016 --> 05:51.000
The secret magic invented
by the prodigy Elfaria.

05:51.071 --> 05:53.056
El Glace Frosse.

05:54.023 --> 05:57.071
As a great feat in creating
twelve original spells,

05:57.071 --> 06:01.013
Elfaria has a serial art named after her
in recognition of this achievement.

06:01.063 --> 06:05.076
And he's using one of the spells
from that series.

06:06.022 --> 06:09.018
El One: Ars Weiss.

06:09.018 --> 06:12.089
A clone spell that creates living
ice sculptures of the caster.

06:12.089 --> 06:15.052
How can you use Elfie's spell?

06:25.045 --> 06:27.053
Because I'm talented.

06:27.053 --> 06:30.079
What other answer do you need?

06:31.022 --> 06:34.029
I learned how to use this spell
all on my own.

06:34.029 --> 06:38.029
It may only be the first of the series,
but I've reached the Magia Vander.

06:38.079 --> 06:41.003
I guess Albis Vina
isn't so special after all.

06:45.022 --> 06:49.072
Someday, I'll strip her of everything.

06:53.064 --> 06:56.019
Julius!

07:07.078 --> 07:12.079
I can move my clones as I wish
and have them cast spells as well.

07:12.079 --> 07:14.054
What's wrong, No-talent?

07:14.088 --> 07:17.092
If you stay still like that,
you're going to lose to them!

07:21.042 --> 07:22.042
And...

07:25.005 --> 07:27.043
What's this?
The attacks stopped?

07:33.093 --> 07:36.081
I can even make a cage like this.

07:36.081 --> 07:38.055
Remote circle?

07:38.055 --> 07:40.082
He made a barrier using
his clones as the anchor.

07:42.011 --> 07:43.082
I'm trapped.

07:46.057 --> 07:51.033
Nothing's easier than hunting
a wild animal on a rampage.

08:00.084 --> 08:03.009
Xelunea Caulis.

08:06.059 --> 08:08.003
It's over.

08:18.035 --> 08:19.048
So, so...

08:19.089 --> 08:21.048
So strong!

08:21.048 --> 08:23.048
He's too strong!

08:23.048 --> 08:28.074
Win the battle without moving.
It's the ideal of any mage.

08:31.049 --> 08:33.087
Julius Reinberg.

08:33.087 --> 08:37.000
It's no wonder that he's able to
earn over 10,000 credits.

08:43.054 --> 08:46.051
Are you watching, scouts?

08:47.009 --> 08:52.051
As you can see, I've flawlessly
mastered Albis Vina's secret ice magic.

08:54.014 --> 09:00.052
I, Julius Reinberg,
will be the successor to Lady Elfaria.

09:03.002 --> 09:05.036
He can use Lady Elfaria's spell.

09:05.036 --> 09:06.053
That's incredible.

09:06.053 --> 09:08.015
Nobody can beat him.

09:08.015 --> 09:10.078
It's all a demonstration.

09:10.078 --> 09:16.008
He took advantage of Will's monster-like
agility to make himself look good.

09:16.008 --> 09:17.079
How clever.

09:18.019 --> 09:18.091
However...

09:18.091 --> 09:22.032
He'll look silly if he loses here.

09:25.054 --> 09:27.055
Wait, it couldn't be...

09:37.068 --> 09:39.056
How did he break free?

09:41.093 --> 09:44.006
Thank you, Julius.

09:44.047 --> 09:47.057
Your spell helped me to cool my head.

09:49.011 --> 09:54.007
I tend to get worked up when it comes
to Elfie, it's a bad habit of mine.

09:54.048 --> 09:56.078
What are you babbling about?

09:56.078 --> 09:59.058
This time, I'll disgrace you for sure!

10:13.018 --> 10:16.043
First of all,
your Ars Weiss isn't perfect.

10:26.009 --> 10:28.048
He hid himself in the first attack,

10:28.048 --> 10:32.082
and then launched his attack
from their blind spot.

10:33.036 --> 10:34.099
Like he did to me.

10:36.016 --> 10:38.002
What was that?!

10:38.002 --> 10:42.002
Will took out two members of Squad 9!

10:45.046 --> 10:47.096
What's going on?!

10:48.004 --> 10:49.071
Look at that.

10:49.071 --> 10:52.088
Julius's clones are falling apart.

10:58.011 --> 11:00.097
You had your friends to help
you control the clones

11:01.064 --> 11:05.064
and were able to cast
Elfie's spell for a moment.

11:06.009 --> 11:08.094
You're not even close to her level.

11:09.004 --> 11:12.094
Damn you!

11:14.028 --> 11:16.007
Julius Reinberg.

11:17.016 --> 11:23.083
Indeed, if he's as good as reported here,

11:24.025 --> 11:26.029
he may be able to become my successor.

11:27.088 --> 11:33.001
But, Sarissa, what I want
isn't a successor.

11:36.034 --> 11:41.072
What I want by my side is a sword.

11:59.004 --> 12:02.028
Your Ars Weiss isn't perfect.

12:02.028 --> 12:04.087
Unlike the autonomous guardians,

12:04.087 --> 12:07.041
Ars Weiss is controlled
completely by the caster.

12:08.004 --> 12:12.067
Your teammates were helping you
control your clones.

12:14.067 --> 12:18.003
You haven't mastered Ars Weiss.

12:20.008 --> 12:26.048
A no-talent who can't even use magic...
Don't you dare lecture me!

12:38.035 --> 12:43.024
I'll freeze your big mouth!

12:57.051 --> 13:00.022
I hate to admit it.

13:00.022 --> 13:05.022
I'm not good enough to control
four clones at once yet.

13:05.089 --> 13:09.069
Without their support,
this spell will drain me fast.

13:10.039 --> 13:11.004
But!

13:11.085 --> 13:15.082
He will never know
which one is the real me.

13:17.052 --> 13:20.057
My clones are just as beautiful as I am.

13:20.057 --> 13:23.002
They match my good looks
and handsomeness.

13:23.002 --> 13:25.007
The disguise is flawless.

13:25.007 --> 13:27.033
There's no way he can tell us apart—

13:31.029 --> 13:32.075
Frall!

13:47.085 --> 13:51.006
How did you know?

13:53.006 --> 13:58.019
The average body temperature of an Ars Weiss
clone is the exact opposite of the caster's.

13:58.019 --> 14:01.057
It's around minus 36 or 37 degrees.

14:01.057 --> 14:04.082
It can be even lower
depending on how it is cast.

14:04.082 --> 14:08.037
If the caster isn't completely in control,
the cold will seep out of the clones.

14:08.037 --> 14:11.075
Just like with Frost Walkers,
ice crystals form around their feet.

14:17.054 --> 14:18.071
Just how?

14:18.071 --> 14:23.097
How could a no-talent like you
know more about this spell than I do?

14:23.097 --> 14:25.097
Tell me!

14:28.051 --> 14:32.077
Because Elfie...
Elfaria was my childhood friend.

14:33.085 --> 14:38.011
We were both abandoned
and we grew up in the same orphanage.

14:38.086 --> 14:43.036
So I know a lot about Elfaria's magic.

14:43.075 --> 14:46.037
I admired it, that's why I studied it.

14:51.012 --> 14:53.008
But I could never reach her.

15:00.063 --> 15:02.026
Don't worry.

15:02.088 --> 15:07.039
Our memories and your hard work

15:07.008 --> 15:10.076
would never go in vain.

15:15.052 --> 15:17.015
That's why, Julius...

15:17.015 --> 15:21.028
I know all the strengths
and weaknesses of Elfie's magic.

15:21.028 --> 15:23.003
That's impossible!

15:23.003 --> 15:25.003
This is Albis Vina's!

15:25.003 --> 15:27.028
Magia Vander's secret magic!

15:27.028 --> 15:31.016
I won't let a no-talent like you mock it!

15:37.079 --> 15:41.004
Julius, you sure are amazing.

15:41.004 --> 15:45.022
No mage has ever been able to
use her magic before.

15:45.022 --> 15:46.047
But...

15:46.089 --> 15:51.001
Ars Weiss is a spell that Elfie created
when she was two years old.

15:53.001 --> 15:55.056
What? Two years old?

15:58.001 --> 16:01.036
So it's not perfect and it can be beaten.

16:01.036 --> 16:03.048
Using that to brag would make you

16:03.091 --> 16:05.094
nothing more than the Naked King!

16:05.094 --> 16:07.028
The Naked King?

16:07.028 --> 16:08.011
Who? Me?

16:08.011 --> 16:08.099
Rather than that...

16:08.099 --> 16:09.099
- Two years old?
- She was an infant.

16:09.099 --> 16:12.066
I was so proud of myself for
learning this spell.

16:16.008 --> 16:19.004
But I'm no better than an infant?

16:35.006 --> 16:38.056
Don't screw with me!

16:46.032 --> 16:48.007
Wow, look at that!

16:48.007 --> 16:49.086
There are more clones!

16:49.086 --> 16:53.078
Five, six, seven...
There are eight Julius!

16:55.099 --> 16:59.041
Did you think four was my limit?

16:59.041 --> 17:00.091
Don't underestimate me!

17:01.056 --> 17:03.092
It doesn't matter
if I can't control them perfectly.

17:03.092 --> 17:07.097
I'll beat you with sheer numbers.

17:07.097 --> 17:11.018
This time, it's your loss!

17:14.081 --> 17:17.031
Sorry, Julius.

17:20.014 --> 17:23.098
I used to get bullied by ten Elfie.

17:27.048 --> 17:30.057
Glace Itier!

17:54.043 --> 17:57.014
Stop him!

18:53.078 --> 18:54.049
Wait!

19:18.063 --> 19:22.077
Will wins against Julius!

19:22.077 --> 19:28.052
What a twist! A no-talent has just beaten
an elite with more than 10,000 credits!

19:29.056 --> 19:31.053
Senior Will!

19:35.028 --> 19:36.024
Will!

19:41.054 --> 19:43.029
Will Serfort.

19:48.029 --> 19:53.026
It's hard to believe, but there's
nothing that stands in his way.

19:53.026 --> 19:56.038
All he has to do is to get the crown.

19:58.093 --> 20:00.003
Good grief.

20:01.001 --> 20:04.018
Do you even know how this game works?

20:04.093 --> 20:09.044
While you two were busy dueling,
I went ahead and picked this up.

20:13.007 --> 20:15.049
How long have they been there?!

20:15.049 --> 20:17.095
The twists just keep on coming!

20:17.095 --> 20:20.057
The winner of Crown Attack is...

20:20.097 --> 20:25.029
Squad 12, led by Wignall Lindor!

20:35.009 --> 20:39.022
It seems the Crown Attack has ended.

20:41.018 --> 20:42.022
Sarissa.

20:43.014 --> 20:46.022
Is there a spell that lets you
go back to the past?

20:46.022 --> 20:48.073
There is no such spell.

20:48.073 --> 20:52.056
How about a spell to erase a memory?

20:52.056 --> 20:55.048
There may be one among
the forbidden arts,

20:55.087 --> 20:57.053
but I would not allow you to use it.

20:58.024 --> 21:02.032
You're wrong, Will!
I wasn't bullying you!

21:02.032 --> 21:07.012
I just wanted you all to myself
so we could play together all the time!

21:08.091 --> 21:13.025
Now all the students know
about my dark past.

21:26.001 --> 21:30.064
That flunkee is even able to win
against Julius.

21:32.094 --> 21:37.028
I will definitely defeat you.

21:37.028 --> 21:38.004
Will!

21:44.015 --> 21:46.045
I'm sorry. They took it.

21:56.025 --> 21:59.013
But I'm able to fulfill the promise.

23:37.065 --> 23:41.036
Next up, Episode 8 of
Wistoria: Wand and Sword,

23:41.078 --> 23:43.069
"Shall we date?"
